  "new_commit_message": "fix: replace ${CLAUDE_SKILL_ROOT} with skill-root-relative paths (#146)\n\n## Problem\n\n`${CLAUDE_SKILL_ROOT}` is used across multiple skills to reference\nbundled scripts and files. This causes two problems in Claude Code:\n\n1. **Permission friction** — variable expansion in bash commands\ntriggers a confirmation prompt\n2. **Runtime failure** — after confirmation, the variable is not set, so\npaths resolve to `/scripts/foo.py` → file not found\n\nReported by Phil in\n[#proj-junior](https://sentry.slack.com/archives/C07P2KGJGG0/p1778225171252819).\n\n## Changes\n\nReplaced all `${CLAUDE_SKILL_ROOT}/...` references with\nskill-root-relative paths (e.g. `scripts/foo.py`, `references/bar.md`)\nper the [Agent Skills spec](https://agentskills.io/specification).\n\n**Affected skills (8 files):**\n- `iterate-pr/SKILL.md` — 14 refs → all converted; updated guidance text\n- `gh-review-requests/SKILL.md` — 2 refs\n- `presentation-creator/SKILL.md` — 4 refs\n- `presentation-creator/references/design-system.md` — 3 refs\n- `skill-scanner/SKILL.md` — 6 refs; updated guidance text\n- `sred-project-organizer/SKILL.md` — 4 refs\n- `skill-writer/SOURCES.md` — changelog entry added\n- `skill-writer/references/registration-validation.md` — updated\nmeta-guidance to recommend against env var path prefixes\n\n## Verification\n\n```bash\n# Only remaining mentions are in skill-writer changelog/meta docs (documenting the change itself)\ngrep -rn \"CLAUDE_SKILL_ROOT\" skills/ --include=\"*.md\"\n```\n\nCloses #145\n\nCo-authored-by: junior[bot] <junior[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>",
